    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a trifecta of high-efficiency plays: **Seiya Suzuki** (67.36), **Corbin Carroll** (64.88), and **Brice Turang** (64.10). **Seiya Suzuki** presents the premier start, benefiting from a favorable 4.66 xERA matchup against Lugo, while **Corbin Carroll** maintains elite status despite the moderate threat posed by Yamamoto, largely due to his premium spot in the order and inherent speed floor. **Brice Turang** serves as our primary catalyst for stolen bases; his 64.10 score is significantly bolstered by his lead-off role and a matchup against a pitcher with a slow delivery, which provides a concrete boost to his stolen base probability\u2014a critical factor given our league's scarcity.\n\nThe optimizer leaned heavily into park and platoon factors to distinguish our marginal starts. **Max Muncy** (62.89) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (60.58) both benefit from favorable wind conditions and a park upgrade, pushing them into the recommended start tier despite facing a capable arm in Bennett. Conversely, the benching of **Cole Young** (39.56) was the most difficult decision of the cycle. While his batting order slot provided a boost, his overall efficiency score failed to clear our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" threshold, falling victim to a combination of a tough park environment and a subpar matchup against Jax.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's rotation. **Austin Riley** (48.58) and **Gabriel Moreno** (53.37) are playing in high-difficulty environments against elite arms like Cole and Yamamoto, respectively. While they are slated to start, their output remains volatile; should weather shift or lineups undergo late revisions, they are the primary candidates for early-game adjustments. Furthermore, with **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** lingering on the IL, our roster flexibility is limited, forcing us to lean on the depth of **Zach McKinstry** to preserve our remaining season game caps while seeking marginal gains in the categories that remain within reach.",
